cookbook/decisions/restart-the-port-from-isaiahs-clean-base.md:55:Source: `user-directive:2026-09-29:update-kaggle-environments-1-32-7`. Isaiah's project took `kaggle-environments` from git HEAD, locked at 1.29.0, which has no Kaggriculture environment. It is now pinned to `==1.32.7` via `uv remove` + `uv add`, which also removes the git source override. 1.32.7's `envs/kaggriculture/kaggriculture.py` has SHA-256 `bc8a5487…`, the engine the vendored Rust kernel targets.
cookbook/decisions/restart-the-port-from-isaiahs-clean-base.md:57:Isaiah's critical pins are unchanged: torch 2.9.0, triton 3.5.0, flash-attn 2.8.3, numpy, pydantic, wandb, mypy. The other 50 lockfile changes are kaggle-environments' own dependency tree (e.g. jax 0.10 → 0.11.2). Checks with 1.32.7: `just prepare` passes, with Rust 155 passed / 2 ignored (Orbit replay and generation parity) and Python 722 passed / 3 skipped.
